  "statement": "GLE1 and UHRF2 are broadly expressed proteins with roles in mRNA export and DNA methylation, respectively, and have no genetic or mechanistic links to psoriasis. EGFL8 possesses strong GWAS associations with psoriasis, but it is located within the highly polymorphic MHC class III region on chromosome 6; its genetic association is a classic case of linkage disequilibrium with the major PSORS1 risk locus (HLA-C*06:02), and there is no evidence that EGFL8 itself plays a functional role in the disease mechanism.",
